course: dictionary
lesson: 2559
title: Deliberately: on purpose or slowly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Deliberately» tells you that someone chose to do something. It is an adverb, made from the adjective «deliberate». Something done deliberately was meant, not an accident. «He broke the cup deliberately» means he meant to break it.
explain: Context decides which meaning fits. «The player made a deliberate foul» means the player planned it. But «He spoke deliberately, one word at a time» means he spoke slowly and carefully, not that he planned anything. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
explain: Often you decide if something was deliberate by asking, «Was it an accident?» In «He is not cleverer than the teachers, and «knowed» is a deliberately wrong word for «known»», the writer chose the wrong word on purpose. The writer meant it, so it is not a mistake.
fact: Deliberately is an adverb. Its adjective is deliberate, as in a deliberate act.
fact: Deliberately means on purpose: you meant to do it, and it was not by accident.
fact: Deliberately can also mean slowly and carefully, as in «He spoke deliberately».
fact: «Knowed» is a deliberately wrong word for «known», so the writer chose it on purpose.
fact: Intentionally is a more formal synonym for on purpose.
exercise: «He broke the cup deliberately, not by accident.» What does deliberately mean here? | Very late at night | *On purpose | Quietly, in the next room | By chance, with nobody to blame
exercise: The referee says, «The player made a deliberate foul.» What does deliberate tell you? | The player was very tired | The game was cancelled | The foul was a lucky accident | *The foul was planned and meant
exercise: «He spoke deliberately, one word at a time.» What does deliberately mean? | *Slowly and carefully | By accident | Very loudly and quickly | Angrily
test: Which word is a formal synonym for deliberately, meaning on purpose? | Accidentally | Suddenly | *Intentionally | Carelessly
test: Which sentence uses deliberately to mean slowly and carefully? | *She turned the page deliberately, careful not to tear it | He tripped deliberately on the stairs | They lost the game deliberately | She ran deliberately to catch the bus
exam: Jayden says, «It was an accident, I did not do it deliberately.» What does he mean? | *He did not do it on purpose | He planned it carefully and meant it | He did it very slowly | His teacher asked him to do it
